       (add-carry-preservation . "No n-bit truncation, wraparound or modulo 2^n; exact output is left-zero-filled to its selected domain width. Explicit Dn/D(2n) identity is retained and is not inferred from normalized magnitude alone.")
       (addition-bridge-scope . "The only newly admitted cross-domain transition is same-domain natural addition overflowing Dn into D(2n); mixed-domain arithmetic, multiplication promotion, signed/rational arithmetic and general coercions remain outside this law.")
